=== Chamber of Deputies ===

All 23 [[Provinces of Argentina|provinces]] and the city of [[Autonomous City of Buenos Aires|Buenos Aires]] held elections to renew half of the [[Argentine Chamber of Deputies|Chamber of Deputies]] (lower house). Each province and the autonomous city elects a number of [[at-large]] representatives on a [[party list]] system roughly proportional to their population, and no province is allotted fewer than five Deputies. The system used to know how many deputies per party in each district is [[D'Hondt method]].

Early projections suggested that President Cristina Kirchner's FpV would increase their representation in the Lower House from 87 seats (out of 257),<ref name=congress>{{cite web|url=http://www.clarin.com/politica/elecciones/camaras-elecciones_CLAFIL20111022_0002.jpg|title=Cómo están las cámaras antes de las elecciones|work=Clarín}}</ref> to around 116; the presence of an estimated ten allies would put them three votes shy of an absolute majority.<ref name=tiempo>{{cite web|url=http://tiempo.elargentino.com/notas/congreso-final-para-grupo-y-presidencia-opositora-senado |title=Congreso: final para el Grupo A y la presidencia opositora en el Senado |work=Tiempo Argentino |url-status=usurped |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111026115656/http://tiempo.elargentino.com/notas/congreso-final-para-grupo-y-presidencia-opositora-senado |archive-date=26 October 2011 }}</ref>

